  "query_preview": "(Sunday through Wednesday):\n\nA wholesale pattern change will be taking place next week,\nproviding more opportunities for some needed rainfall. The\nsynoptic models continue to develop a large, cutoff upper low \nover the central Plains early next week, with an associated\nsurface cyclone intensifying. GFS solutions are the more \nintense of the group, while the European solutions are slower \nand more influenced by a separate low skirting the northern \nborder of Minnesota. The latter camp would suggest more dry\nweather Sunday and Monday, while the former provides more\nnumerous rain chances from Sunday all the way through next\nThursday. In any event, this does appear to be the best rain\nchances we have seen in some time. Overnight LREF guidance shows\na 50-60% chance of seeing more than an inch of rain in areas\nwest of I-57, though this has trended down some from the\nprevious run. The fine details of cutoff lows are always a\nchallenge to pin down this far in advance, though. \n\nMorning NBM guidance came in warmer for early next week, with\nmainly lower 70s for highs, but clouds and rain extent will\nprobably temper this down somewhat.",
